Z||000031||Songman||12-18-2000||02:00 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>79 Cadillac 425 Cu in BB , HO built by ASC as a Demo car , sold to my Grandfather</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I was gonna ask how you came across a 1979 Cadillac with a 425 when 1978 was the last year Cadillac put out a big block car but now I see that this is an ASC-built car. I guess they might have put a 1978 model engine in one of their cars.<P>I have a 1978 Sedan de Ville that has the 425 in it. It was ordered in late 1977 by my great uncle as a Christmas present for his wife. Now I have it and it has over 260,000 miles on it and still runs strong for a big car. Just have to make sure and not pass a gas station without stopping!<P>||||reg||3
